  description: A nebula is a vast cloud of gas and dust found in space. Some nebulae
    are regions where gravity brings material together to form new stars, while others
    are created when stars release material into space near the end of their lives.
  interestingFact: The Orion Nebula is one of the closest major star-forming regions
    to Earth and can be seen with the naked eye under dark skies.
